Notebook[{
Cell["Hypermatrix", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"5109cd9d-126a-ab4b-9d95-7cf0254b592e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c115ea16-fea0-114a-8d24-914596884cee"],
 " ",
 "represents the given arrays as a hypermatrix, holding them in canonical \
order."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"72549289-fa3c-1643-807d-4317e2273455"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"arr1", ",", " ", "arr2", ",", " ", "..."}], "]"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f50cff6-e581-f948-afa8-b99e0bf08840"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"ad90a85b-7844-7747-bd87-d52b8697cecb"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"09a875d9-44a7-d04d-abc0-81acad59a05f"],

Cell["\<\
The arrays are ordered by array order, lowest first; then by dimensions, \
shorter first, compared term by term; then by symmetry, taking \"Symmetric\" \
before \"Cyclic\" before \"Rigid\".\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4e619182-2132-3e44-9826-3aae8b767d82"],

Cell["\<\
Two arrays alike in all three are put in the Wolfram Language's own canonical \
order, so that a hypermatrix is a function of the set of arrays it was given \
and of nothing else. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"242cebda-d611-9749-bf85-239921570df5"],

Cell["\<\
An irregular array is necessarily \"Rigid\", since only a regular array can \
carry a symmetry, so the symmetry criterion separates the regular arrays \
among themselves.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b4b49a9a-0509-9b40-88e2-9e1559ee71c1"],

Cell["\<\
Arrays of any kind of entry sit together freely. Raw entries given in place \
of an array are promoted to an ArrayObject.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8670890b-edb7-0d48-ae2c-4960d8cc33b4"],

Cell["\<\
Length gives the number of arrays, and Normal the entries of each of them in \
order.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5a172c80-a131-204e-9390-6442abaeec38"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"68077c35-c922-a942-bdf5-c9185d6f7b86"],

Cell["The arrays are sorted whatever order they are given in:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"f4d38038-9d8e-8546-88c5-63d5bc80b442"],

Cell["\<\
hm = Hypermatrix[{
   ArrayObject[Array[1 &, {2, 2, 2}], \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2}],
   ArrayObject[{1, 2, 3}],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Symmetric\"],
   ArrayObject[{{1, 2}, {2, 1}}, \"Cyclic\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"71261418-5f4f-784a-b9e7-91d76f2c23f3"],

